Energy needs for symptomatic HIV-positive patients can be calculated using equations like the Harris-Benedict or Schofield equations, adjusted for stress factors. For asymptomatic patients, energy needs increase by 10% to maintain weight and activity levels. For symptomatic patients, energy needs increase by 20–30% due to disease progression.  

