","Both the National Cancer Institute (NCI) and the American Cancer Society (ACS) offer a wealth of educational resources for patients and their families navigating end-of-life care. 

**National Cancer Institute (NCI):**

* **Facing Cancer:** This section of the NCI website provides comprehensive information on various aspects of cancer, including end-of-life care. It covers topics like:
    * **Advance care planning:** Making decisions about your care preferences in advance.
    * **Palliative care:** Managing symptoms and improving quality of life for people with serious illnesses.
    * **Hospice care:** Providing comfort and support for people in the final stages of life.
    * **Bereavement support:** Coping with the loss of a loved one.
    * **Resources for caregivers:** Information and support for those caring for someone with cancer.
* **Cancer.gov:** The main NCI website also has a search function where you can find specific information on end-of-life care, such as ""hospice care"" or ""advance directives.""
* **NCI's Cancer Information Service:** You can call 1-800-4-CANCER (1-800-422-6237) to speak with a trained specialist who can answer your questions and provide personalized guidance.

**American Cancer Society (ACS):**

* **End-of-Life Care:** This section of the ACS website offers resources on:
    * **Making decisions about end-of-life care:** Understanding your options and making informed choices.
    * **Talking to your doctor about end-of-life care:** Communicating your wishes and preferences.
    * **Finding hospice care:** Locating hospice providers in your area.
    * **Supporting a loved one at the end of life:** Providing comfort and care during this difficult time.
* **Cancer.org:** The main ACS website also has a wealth of information on end-of-life care, including articles, videos, and support groups.
* **ACS's 24/7 Helpline:** You can call 1-800-227-2345 to speak with a trained specialist who can provide information, support, and resources.

**Additional Resources:**

* **National Hospice and Palliative Care Organization (NHPCO):** https://www.nhpco.org/
* **Compassion & Choices:** https://compassionandchoices.org/

Remember, it's important to have open and honest conversations with your loved ones and healthcare providers about your wishes for end-of-life care. These organizations can provide valuable information and support to help you make informed decisions and navigate this challenging time.
