- **Cancer:** NK cells play a crucial role in early cancer detection and elimination. Their dysfunction can increase the risk of cancer development and progression.
- **Autoimmune Diseases:**  While NK cells normally help regulate immune responses, their dysregulation can contribute to autoimmune disorders.

