* Mass of S = (moles of S) * (molar mass of S)
* Mass of S = 1.797 mol * 32 g/mol = 57.5 g

**6. Calculate the mass of residual gases:**

* Mass of residual gases = (total mass of air) - (mass of oxygen reacted)
* Mass of residual gases = 250 g - 57.5 g = 192.5 g



**Therefore:**

* **250 g of sulfur should be burnt to remove the oxygen from 250 g of air.**
* **The weight of residual gases in the air will be 192.5 g.**
