","Here's how to find the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of the matrix [D] using Jacobi's method:

**1.  Initialization:**

*   Start with an initial guess for the orthogonal matrix [R].  A common choice is the identity matrix:
    [R]<sub>0</sub> = [I] =  \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}

